   = note: function values have no run-time representation: a value chosen by run-time control flow is compiled to a selector over a finite set of closures known at compile time
   = note: a variable that is not itself a function can hold a function value chosen at run time only if it holds a value with a function value in it before the branch or loop
   = note: help: give `m` such a value before the branch or loop, and use the same constructor for `m` on every path
